+# PR #742 audit response
+
+**Upstream base:** `9f6cfcf` (PR #742 merged as `21cc329`).
+**Scope:** independent verification and remediation of audit findings D1–D9.
+**Status:** all source findings adjudicated; required fixes implemented; final CI validation recorded below.
+
+## Executive verdict
+
+The audit was useful, but its claims were treated as hypotheses and reprobed against the merged compiler. D1, D2, D4, D6, and D7 were confirmed; D5 is part of D2; D3 and D9 identified real validation gaps; D8 correctly requested a stack/budget cross-reference. The mid-line `#embed` standards objection was also correct: LCCC retains that existing behavior as an explicitly labeled extension, not as standard C23 syntax.
+
+## Finding-by-finding adjudication
+
+| Finding | Verdict | Remediation and evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| **D1 — right-recursive expressions not counted** | **Confirmed (High)** | Added frame-budget wrappers to `parse_expr`, `parse_assignment_expr`, and `parse_conditional_expr`, covering comma RHS, simple/compound assignment RHS, and standard/GNU conditional recursion. I rebuilt the unmodified base `9f6cfcf` in a clean worktree and verified all three valid 500k inputs: comma, assignment, and conditional each aborted with rc=134 and Rust's stack-overflow text but no compiler diagnostic. After the fix, the durable gate's three valid 500k cases each return rc=1 with exactly one `expression nesting too deep (exceeds 32768 parser frames)` diagnostic; no abort, signal, hang, or diagnostic flood. The previously overstated “every recursive parser entry point” claim was replaced with an explicit maintained entry-point contract. |
+| **D2 — #embed metadata clamp / stream probe and read behavior** | **Confirmed (Medium–High)** | Replaced metadata-sized allocation/read logic with `Read::take`-bounded incremental reads. Metadata is used as an upper bound only for regular files; `st_size == 0` or a misleading positive size on a device/FIFO/proc resource never clamps the stream. `EMBED_READ_CAP` is 512 MiB; over-cap requests diagnose rather than silently truncate. On Linux/Android and Darwin/BSD, resources open with `O_NONBLOCK`; unsupported Unix hosts reject FIFOs cleanly instead of blocking in `open`. Include and embed path resolution now use separate cache modes, so a regular-file-only `__has_include` miss cannot poison `__has_embed`. Probes use metadata only, reject directories, and report existing streams as Found without opening/consuming them. The gate verifies `/dev/zero limit(16)` yields 16 zero bytes, `__has_embed` is 1, `__has_include` is 0, directories probe NotFound, and a FIFO without a writer completes through `if_empty`. A sparse regular file just over the cap verifies immediate rejection without reading the file. The three existing hostile limit/offset cases remain millisecond-fast. |
+| **D3 — parser admission not tested through later phases** | **Valid gap; closed** | Added `scripts/check_nesting_pipeline_boundaries.py` and wired it into `ci_local.sh` and hosted CI. We binary-searched the maximum admitted source depth for each exact generator on the `-O1` fastbuild compiler, then compile-linked-ran at floor(95%): expression 1151/1212, block 3891/4096, initializer 31104/32742, record 1944/2047. Record layout is forced by a global object and `sizeof`, avoiding a lazy typedef-only false pass. All four cases compile, link, and run correctly with zero compiler/linker warnings; no budget was lowered because the full pipeline survives these boundaries. |
+| **D4 — underline clamp off by one and no pure geometry tests** | **Confirmed** | The caret is printed at `caret_pad`; the rendered line has `shown_len` source/marker characters. The available underline width is `shown_len.saturating_sub(caret_pad) + 1`; the old clamp dropped that final column. Extracted the window, character-count, and squiggle arithmetic into pure functions and added 13 unit tests covering ASCII, UTF-8/multibyte, line start/end, window edges/markers, and the end-of-line regression. |
+| **D5 — #embed probing is inconsistent for special resources** | **Confirmed; subsumed by D2** | The special-file-aware resolver and `probe_embed` change make the query non-destructive and consistent for resource existence: only directories are categorically rejected; regular-file size can yield Empty; streams are Found without a read. The `/dev/zero`, directory, and FIFO probe cases are in the durable gate. |
+| **D6 — executable bits on Python files without shebangs** | **Confirmed** | Removed execute permission from exactly these 11 files: `tests/corpus/test_delivery_contracts.py`, `test_diagnostic_contracts.py`, `test_matching_exhaustive.py`, `test_native_diagnostic_adapter.py`, `test_redteam_boundaries.py`, `test_regression_oracle_contracts.py`, `test_result_invariants.py`, `test_selection_contracts.py`, `test_snapshot_contracts.py`, `test_workload_extraction_safety.py`, and `tests/linker/i386_userspace.py`. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/corpus -p 'test_*.py'` passed all 294 tests. |
+| **D7 — stale names, paths, and review comments** | **Confirmed within the requested scope** | Updated the deep-nesting gate's budget name and stale PR/F5 labels; rewrote the `#embed` adversarial fixture comment to describe the current cap/stream contract; removed the session-local absolute report and staging paths from the touched FOLLOWUP document; and updated the EDG action register so E5's parser-budget alternative and E7's landed miner/index plus seed corpus are accurately recorded. The audit's repository-wide literal absolute-scratch-path grep is not a feasible acceptance test: unrelated pre-existing harness scripts intentionally use that scratch default. Hygiene was applied to the files changed for this finding, without rewriting those unrelated scripts. |
+| **D8 — parser frame budgets disconnected from thread stack** | **Confirmed** | `src/lib.rs::compiler_main` now cross-references the expression/initializer, block, and type budgets; each budget's rationale in `src/frontend/parser/parse.rs` points back to the 64 MiB `STACK_SIZE`. The parser-frame unit test uses the same 64 MiB stack as production (the Rust test harness's default 2 MiB stack is not the compiler's supported configuration). The pipeline-boundary gate pins the corresponding admitted depths. |
+| **D9 — insufficient unit-test density** | **Valid gap; closed** | Added 13 diagnostic-geometry tests, 4 parser-frame lifecycle/one-diagnostic tests, and 2 bounded embed-read tests (including `/dev/zero` and sparse-file cap behavior). The library suite and compiler-free corpus contract suite were rerun; final totals are in the validation section. |
+
+## Standards dispute: mid-line `#embed`
+
+The audit is correct. C23 §6.10.1 requires the `#` preprocessing token that starts a directive to be the first preprocessing token on its logical line (after permitted whitespace/newline). §6.10.15 defines `#embed` but provides no exception to §6.10.1. The normative text is available in the [ISO/IEC 9899:2024 mirror](https://cigix.me/c23), §§6.10.1 and 6.10.15.
+
+LCCC's existing `{ #embed "file" }`-style mid-line splicing remains supported for compatibility, but is now labeled a **LCCC extension** in code comments and fixtures. It is not claimed as standard C23. A pedantic-only warning was not added: this tree has no `-pedantic` warning category/plumbing, and the preprocessor does not receive the `WarningConfig`; adding the warning correctly would require new option/configuration and `-Werror` integration, so it is not a cheap local change. Unconditional warnings would be incorrect for the existing extension users.
+
+## Validation
+
+- LCCC rebuilt via `scripts/build_lccc_fast.sh` (`fastbuild`, `-O1`, `-j2`); the build and lint logs had **zero warnings**.
+- `scripts/ci_local.sh --fast`: **153 passed, 0 failed, 5 slow gates skipped**. The skipped gates are not claimed as a full CI-equivalent run; the working tree has the recorded fast-mode stamp only.
+- The CI cargo-test gate: **4034 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored** (includes all 19 new unit tests).
+- `scripts/check_deep_nesting_robustness.py`: **17/17** crash/legality/semantic cases pass, including all three 500k D1 chains and the `/dev/zero` + FIFO smoke folded into the existing embed slot.
+- `scripts/check_nesting_pipeline_boundaries.py`: **4/4** cases compile, link, and run at 94.97–95.00% of measured admitted source depth.
+- `tests/corpus` compiler-free contract suite: **294 passed** after the exact mode changes.
+- Script-import, CI/workflow-shell, and CI/local gate-parity checks passed after the new boundary gate was wired into both local and hosted CI.
+- The snapshot ledger records each validated implementation, hygiene, and final-evidence batch; the latest snapshot contains the complete upstream-applicable patch.
